   "source": [
    "# Getting started\n",
    "\n",
    "A starting point for exploratory work. It imports only the\n",
    "`{{ project.package_name }}` package and modules that ship with Python, so\n",
    "it runs anywhere the project is installed.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Before committing any notebook**, restart the kernel and clear every\n",
    "output. `uv run --locked poe notebook:check` enforces this: it re-executes a\n",
    "copy of each notebook and fails if a cell carries a stored output or\n",
    "execution count."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "version",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from {{ project.package_name }} import __version__\n",
    "\n",
    "print(__version__)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "layout",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Where things live\n",
    "\n",
    "The generated project reserves these project-root directories for local or\n",
    "generated working material. Git ignores their contents and nothing creates\n",
    "them automatically -- add each one when you first need it.\n",
    "\n",
    "| Directory | Holds |\n",
    "| --- | --- |\n",
    "| `data/raw/` | Immutable source data, exactly as received |\n",
    "| `data/interim/` | Partially transformed data |\n",
    "| `data/processed/` | Final datasets ready for modelling |\n",
    "| `models/` | Trained and serialised models |\n",
    "| `artifacts/` | Generated reports, figures, and run outputs |\n",
    "\n",
    "Keep datasets, trained models, and credentials out of version control."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "summary",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import statistics\n",
    "\n",
    "# A handful of literal values stand in for a real measurement series.\n",
    "observations = [0.12, 0.31, 0.08, 0.45, 0.22]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"count:\", len(observations))\n",
    "print(\"mean:\", round(statistics.mean(observations), 4))\n",
    "print(\"stdev:\", round(statistics.stdev(observations), 4))"
   ]
  }
